# Keep the build context to what the image actually needs: Go sources plus
# go.mod/go.sum. The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so everything not excluded here
# is uploaded to the daemon and cached as a layer input — a large context slows
# every build and invalidates the cache on unrelated edits.

# Personal scratch area — never built, never shipped, never uploaded anywhere.
atlas-PYTHON/

.git/
.github/
.claude/
.vscode/
.devcontainer/

# Front-end: built separately and deployed as static files, not into this image.
ui/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/

# Docs, planning, governance, research — none of it is compiled.
docs/
agents/
context/
rfc/
archive/
lab/
JUNK_DOCS_MD/
*.md
!README.md

# Local build outputs and state that must never end up in an image.
# Root-anchored (leading /) ON PURPOSE: a bare `atlas-server` also matches
# the cmd/atlas-server SOURCE DIRECTORY, which broke the Railway build with
# "stat /src/cmd/atlas-server: directory not found". These entries are meant
# to exclude stray built binaries at the repo root, never source packages.
/atlas-server
/atlas-gate
*.test
*.out
*.pem
*.key
/state.json
/atlas-state.json
